.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files
#
# The four per-slot files ARE TRACKED, deliberately. This repo builds FOUR
# deployments from one codebase, and these are the files they run:
#
#   .env.qa.ca    -> qa.cartzii.ca        .env.prod.ca  -> www.cartzii.ca
#   .env.qa.us    -> qa.cartzii.com       .env.prod.us  -> www.cartzii.com
#
# The deploy does `git reset --hard`, so editing them here and pushing is how
# a storefront's config changes. Editing them on the server does nothing.
#
# THE TRADE-OFF, STATED PLAINLY: they hold real values, and git history keeps
# every version forever. Anyone with read access to this repo gets them, and
# deleting a file later does not remove it from history. Every secret ever
# committed here must be rotated before public launch, and Stripe LIVE keys
# should stay out of the .env.prod.* files until then.
#
# .env.local stays ignored: it is yours, not a deployment's. Keep it that way
# — Next loads .env.local and .env.production during ANY build, so a stray
# file of either name silently beats the per-slot one on a plain
# `next build`, which is why the ignore below is a blanket one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!.env.qa.ca
!.env.qa.us
!.env.prod.ca
!.env.prod.us

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
